we could talk to?

753
00:31:22,248 --> 00:31:24,217
Eight years later...
[Chuckling]

754
00:31:24,250 --> 00:31:27,987
So, anyway, that's what
really got me interested
in stamp collecting.

755
00:31:28,020 --> 00:31:29,688
Of course,
I've always loved the theater.

756
00:31:29,722 --> 00:31:31,390
Just shut up.

757
00:31:33,292 --> 00:31:35,562
[Mock grunting]

758
00:31:35,595 --> 00:31:38,063
Hey, no boat.

759
00:31:38,097 --> 00:31:41,267
That's my scratching tree,
you jerks.

760
00:31:43,168 --> 00:31:46,505
Uh, not that tree.

761
00:31:49,042 --> 00:31:52,145
- [Snickers]
- Uh, fred, did I mention
that I have a boat?

762
00:31:52,178 --> 00:31:54,680
- Sorry.
- No.

763
00:31:54,713 --> 00:31:57,650
Oh, now they're
just showing off.

764
00:31:57,683 --> 00:32:00,320
Oh, now, what did they
chop the sail out of?

765
00:32:00,353 --> 00:32:03,022
- Oh, they cut the wood
real thin. Really.
- Uh-huh.

766
00:32:03,055 --> 00:32:07,327
May the sun light the way
to bring you safely home again.

767
00:32:07,360 --> 00:32:09,928
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Can the balloon juice, gramps.
We're outta here.

768
00:32:09,962 --> 00:32:14,000
Hey, shouldn't we patch
the bottom first?

769
00:32:14,033 --> 00:32:16,668
I just pray there aren't
no portages.

770
00:32:18,203 --> 00:32:22,675
- Oh, boy.
- The stay puft marshmallow man
in chains?

771
00:32:22,708 --> 00:32:24,610
Kinky.

772
00:32:24,643 --> 00:32:26,512
It's giant sweetbreads.

773
00:32:26,545 --> 00:32:29,582
It's body wars.

774
00:32:29,615 --> 00:32:32,618
Someone has come to visit us!

775
00:32:32,652 --> 00:32:35,688
Quick, pick up the place,
make yourself presentable!

776
00:32:35,722 --> 00:32:38,023
- [Male voice] Where?
- [Male voice #2] Over here.

777
00:32:38,057 --> 00:32:41,660
- Near me.
- What, it's a bag
of homer simpsons?

778
00:32:41,693 --> 00:32:43,697
- Who are you?
- [Female voice] We are winds.

779
00:32:43,730 --> 00:32:45,365
Wait. One at a time, please.
Come on.

780
00:32:45,398 --> 00:32:49,335
- --The wind?
- [Female voice] Yes.
I am the south wind.

781
00:32:49,368 --> 00:32:51,570
Do you provide a service
of some sort?

782
00:32:51,603 --> 00:32:53,072
[Male voice]
I am the west wind.

783
00:32:53,105 --> 00:32:56,075
[Male voice #2]
And i-- I am the east wind.

784
00:32:56,108 --> 00:33:00,347
Put your teeth in!
I can't understand you!

785
00:33:00,380 --> 00:33:02,282
Are you the north wind?

786
00:33:02,315 --> 00:33:05,585
[Male voice #3]
No. I am the mist.

787
00:33:05,618 --> 00:33:09,155
I'm relative humidity.
It's not so much the heat
as it is me.

788
00:33:09,188 --> 00:33:12,325
♪ I'm the summer wind
come blowin' in ♪

789
00:33:12,358 --> 00:33:13,793
♪♪ [humming]

790
00:33:15,995 --> 00:33:18,197
- And you-- which one are you?
- [Mock chuckling]

791
00:33:18,230 --> 00:33:20,065
Oh, me?
I'm just the laundry.

792
00:33:20,098 --> 00:33:22,235
[Male voice #4]
I am the north wind.

793
00:33:22,268 --> 00:33:26,538
- Call me sandy.
- I was born among
the ice floes.

794
00:33:26,572 --> 00:33:29,775
Oh, that's fine, thank you.
[Chuckling]

795
00:33:29,808 --> 00:33:31,810
[North wind]
Please let me out.

796
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:33,813
Yeah, I didn't ask
for a biography.

797
00:33:33,847 --> 00:33:37,283
Very well.
I will let you out.

798
00:33:37,317 --> 00:33:40,753
So, this is where I find you,
my little pet.

799
00:33:40,787 --> 00:33:42,755
Um, we weren't kissing.
We were just talking.

800
00:33:42,788 --> 00:33:45,692
Perhaps you need
something to amuse you.

801
00:33:45,725 --> 00:33:49,395
Just come with me.
I'll find something
for you to do.

802
00:33:49,428 --> 00:33:53,032
I've got one of those
little pool tables
I bought at brookstone.

803
00:33:53,065 --> 00:33:55,468
- You'll love it.
- Throw my prisoner in chains!

804
00:33:55,502 --> 00:33:57,770
All right!
Some orders we like to get.
[Chuckling]

805
00:33:57,803 --> 00:34:00,372
- [Shouting]
- Yeah.

806
00:34:05,845 --> 00:34:08,380
Deep thoughts.

807
00:34:08,413 --> 00:34:10,483
Oh, walleye chop.

808
00:34:10,517 --> 00:34:12,685
I'd better get out there.

809
00:34:12,718 --> 00:34:14,987
Erik's small cigars.

810
00:34:15,020 --> 00:34:17,523
Inconceivable.
They're gaining on us.

811
00:34:17,557 --> 00:34:21,693
- Oh, the keg's here.
- Ah, he's come,
as I said he would.

812
00:34:21,727 --> 00:34:23,963
Do you see his boat
approaching our shore?

813
00:34:23,997 --> 00:34:26,098
Do you hear the waves
bringing him nearer?

814
00:34:26,132 --> 00:34:28,968
Come. Wake up.
Run to the beach
and welcome him.

815
00:34:29,002 --> 00:34:32,037
You're the boss.
You're the queen of everything.
Okay.

816
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:34,973
Smiles, everyone! Smiles!
[Chuckles]

817
00:34:35,007 --> 00:34:37,377
Eh...

818
00:34:37,410 --> 00:34:39,512
Hey, do you have a dock
or something?

819
00:34:39,545 --> 00:34:41,847
We'd really appreciate it!

820
00:34:41,880 --> 00:34:43,515
[Chuckles]
Look at that boat.

821
00:34:43,548 --> 00:34:46,718
- What, did you carve it
out of a tree?
- Shut up! Shut up!

822
00:34:46,752 --> 00:34:48,955
Boat.

823
00:34:48,988 --> 00:34:51,190
Mistress, oh, you were right.

824
00:34:51,223 --> 00:34:52,892
The boat
is bringing lemminkainen--

825
00:34:52,925 --> 00:34:54,393
- mmm! [Smacking lips]
- ...And his friend,

826
00:34:54,427 --> 00:34:57,163
the immortal
blacksmith illmarinen.

827
00:34:57,197 --> 00:34:59,765
- Greetings for all!
- Hi.

828
00:34:59,798 --> 00:35:01,900
Who accepts the challenge
that I have brought?

829
00:35:01,933 --> 00:35:04,103
- Nope. Can't. Got a bad knee.
- I did the last challenge.

830
00:35:04,137 --> 00:35:06,338
I have come to free
the maiden annikki.

831
00:35:06,372 --> 00:35:08,773
- I am here with her brother.
- Uh, tony.

832
00:35:08,808 --> 00:35:11,643
- You are no coward? Then fight!
- Noel coward?

833
00:35:11,677 --> 00:35:14,713
If your power
can protect you from my arrow.

834
00:35:14,747 --> 00:35:16,815
Yes, my power is great.

835
00:35:16,848 --> 00:35:19,685
Uh, it's not that fun
going to grandma's anymore.

836
00:35:19,718 --> 00:35:22,888
Magic and charms
and terrible spells--

837
00:35:22,922 --> 00:35:24,990
enough to drive you back
into the boiling home

838
00:35:25,023 --> 00:35:27,260
from which you come,
you blundering fool.

839
00:35:27,293 --> 00:35:29,628
That's enough of that.
You imagine we've come here

840
00:35:29,662 --> 00:35:31,397
to listen to
an old woman raving?

841
00:35:31,430 --> 00:35:33,967
- That's why most people come.
- Now, do you accept
the challenge,

842
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:35,935
or will you give up
my sister without it?

843
00:35:35,968 --> 00:35:37,437
- Take the curtain.
- Go for the box.

844
00:35:37,470 --> 00:35:39,605
I will not give up annikki.

845
00:35:39,638 --> 00:35:41,840
- ...bust the witch's bosom.
- No, wait!

846
00:35:41,873 --> 00:35:43,375
- Let me take off my girdle.
- Wait now!

847
00:35:43,408 --> 00:35:45,578
I will give
your maiden back to you

848
00:35:45,612 --> 00:35:48,380
if you perform
two simple tasks for me.

849
00:35:48,413 --> 00:35:50,817
- Aw, this bites. Let's blow.
- What are they?

850
00:35:50,850 --> 00:35:52,952
Pick up my dry cleaning
and call the vet.

851
00:35:52,985 --> 00:35:55,253
I have a field
overrun with snakes,

852
00:35:55,287 --> 00:35:57,690
and he must first plow it.

853
00:35:57,723 --> 00:36:00,760
- All right.
- It's weird, but...

854
00:36:00,793 --> 00:36:02,895
- Tell me where your field is.
- Come on.

855
00:36:02,928 --> 00:36:06,265
COME ON, GOOD LEMMINKäINEN.

856
00:36:07,667 --> 00:36:09,635
Don't wait up, erik,
if you know what I mean.

857
00:36:09,668 --> 00:36:12,372
- Say, that is cold.
- [Laughs]

858
00:36:15,207 --> 00:36:17,175
You see it before you.

859
00:36:17,210 --> 00:36:19,312
I see an el greco.

860
00:36:19,345 --> 00:36:21,813
[Louhi]
A field of snakes.

861
00:36:21,847 --> 00:36:23,715
Hey, kevin costner's
in that, isn't he?

862
00:36:23,748 --> 00:36:26,718
- No, this is the dirty version.
- Oh.

863
00:36:26,752 --> 00:36:30,522
I want a plow, and I must have
a powerful horse with it.

864
00:36:30,557 --> 00:36:32,525
Hey,
I'm the curse boss here.

865
00:36:32,558 --> 00:36:35,493
...to feed one of my horses
to those snakes?

866
00:36:35,527 --> 00:36:38,197
Needs a horse.
I will build him a horse.

867
00:36:38,230 --> 00:36:40,232
I'll make it out of a tree.

868
00:36:40,265 --> 00:36:42,167
Uh--oh.

869
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:43,635
Horse chestnut.
[Laughs]

870
00:36:43,668 --> 00:36:44,637
Oh, mistress.

871
00:36:44,670 --> 00:36:46,605
Don't call me that
in public.

872
00:36:48,373 --> 00:36:52,077
You must not allow illmarinen
to build that horse.

873
00:36:52,110 --> 00:36:55,582
He'll be sure to plow the field,
and they will take annikki.

874
00:36:55,615 --> 00:36:58,183
And illmarinen will refuse
to make us a sampo.

875
00:36:58,217 --> 00:36:59,718
Have patience.

876
00:36:59,752 --> 00:37:02,322
He won't be able
to carry her away.

877
00:37:02,355 --> 00:37:04,123
Now, slip into that
stable boy suit

878
00:37:04,157 --> 00:37:05,958
and meet me later
down by the [whispers].

879
00:37:05,992 --> 00:37:09,295
[Laughs]
Yes, mistress. Oh, my.

880
00:37:11,963 --> 00:37:12,998
Ooh. Uh-oh.

881
00:37:13,032 --> 00:37:14,133
Wow.

882
00:37:14,167 --> 00:37:16,402
And the sculling crew
takes to the lake.

883
00:37:16,435 --> 00:37:18,637
We've got to get
organized.

884
00:37:18,670 --> 00:37:22,308
Attica! Attica! Attica!

885
00:37:22,342 --> 00:37:24,410
It's the oslo riots.

886
00:37:24,443 --> 00:37:27,112
Hey, uh, that's not very smart
when you're in the boat.

887
00:37:27,145 --> 00:37:28,713
He's pounding
the air there.

888
00:37:28,747 --> 00:37:29,715
It's an air hammer.

889
00:37:29,748 --> 00:37:32,285
[Laughter]

890
00:37:32,318 --> 00:37:34,587
Hey, we're goin' over
to sven's after, huh?

891
00:37:34,620 --> 00:37:35,755
Want to?

892
00:37:36,822 --> 00:37:37,790
Huh?

893
00:37:37,823 --> 00:37:39,458
Suddenly it's flashdance.

894
00:37:39,492 --> 00:37:42,762
♪ He's a steel town's fan
on a saturday night ♪

895
00:37:42,795 --> 00:37:45,430
Weird.

896
00:37:45,463 --> 00:37:47,032
Okay. Okay.

897
00:37:47,065 --> 00:37:50,402
If he can make a horse,
why'd he have to cut
that tree down?

898
00:37:50,435 --> 00:37:52,103
Mm.

899
00:37:52,137 --> 00:37:53,838
Yeah, well,
now I just sit back

900
00:37:53,872 --> 00:37:55,908
and rake in the praise,
pretty much.

901
00:37:55,942 --> 00:37:58,243
Hello, daddy.
[Laughs]

902
00:37:58,277 --> 00:37:59,912
The tristar logo's ready.

903
00:37:59,945 --> 00:38:01,580
He's...

904
00:38:01,613 --> 00:38:03,582
Safe.

905
00:38:07,085 --> 00:38:10,188
♪ They ran callin'
wildfire ♪

906
00:38:10,222 --> 00:38:12,692
♪ whoo ♪

907
00:38:12,725 --> 00:38:16,362
Ouch. Phew. Stingy.
That's still hot.

908
00:38:16,395 --> 00:38:18,697
Hello.
I'm from the temp agency.

909
00:38:18,730 --> 00:38:21,100
I'm your horse
for the day.

910
00:38:22,402 --> 00:38:25,403
Oh. Speed the plow.

911
00:38:25,437 --> 00:38:28,840
Hey, good timing.
Boy, we work good together.

912
00:38:28,873 --> 00:38:32,412
Could you rub some solarcaine
on me, please?

913
00:38:33,478 --> 00:38:36,548
A horse.
We didn't plan on that.

914
00:38:36,582 --> 00:38:39,585
Would someone please
turn the wagner off?

915
00:38:39,618 --> 00:38:42,455
Hey, I think he just
invented the mobil logo.

916
00:38:42,488 --> 00:38:44,423
Oh. Neat.

917
00:38:46,792 --> 00:38:48,993
♪ Doo doo doo doo doo
doo doo doo doo doo ♪

918
00:38:49,028 --> 00:38:50,628
Ew.

919
00:38:50,662 --> 00:38:51,897
Yech.

920
00:38:51,930 --> 00:38:53,932
Snakies.

921
00:38:53,965 --> 00:38:56,202
It's kind of a goofy,
scandinavian double-dare.

922
00:38:56,235 --> 00:38:58,170
[Laughs]

923
00:38:59,705 --> 00:39:01,273
Oh, man.
It's a puppet. Look.

924
00:39:01,307 --> 00:39:02,842
He's being attacked
by a woozle.

925
00:39:02,875 --> 00:39:04,310
[Laughs]

926
00:39:04,343 --> 00:39:06,978
Yeah, they're--they're all
yellin' "fake." Ha!

927
00:39:07,012 --> 00:39:09,848
And now I'd like to do my
nastassja kinski impression.

928
00:39:09,882 --> 00:39:11,150
I'll just take
off my clothes.

929
00:39:11,183 --> 00:39:12,852
[Laughs]

930
00:39:12,885 --> 00:39:15,153
I knew they'd "worm"
their way into the film.

931
00:39:15,187 --> 00:39:16,488
[Laughs]
Worm--

932
00:39:16,522 --> 00:39:18,257
snakes.

933
00:39:18,290 --> 00:39:21,393
You know, I wonder if that horse
comes in any other colors.

934
00:39:22,962 --> 00:39:25,230
Uh, he's the enemy,
but you gotta admire him.

935
00:39:25,263 --> 00:39:26,932
Yup. Yup.
Tip your cap.

936
00:39:26,965 --> 00:39:28,767
Uh, pretty much.

937
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:31,170
Get a look at this,
huh?

938
00:39:31,203 --> 00:39:33,905
Now, let's go in and see
if mom's got dinner ready.

939
00:39:36,075 --> 00:39:38,177
Oh, great.
We can plant more snakes now.

940
00:39:38,210 --> 00:39:39,745
[Laughs]

941
00:39:41,213 --> 00:39:43,382
All right.
I've finished plowing
your field.

942
00:39:43,415 --> 00:39:44,650
Planted now with care.

943
00:39:44,683 --> 00:39:45,818
[Grunts]

944
00:39:45,852 --> 00:39:48,487
And may the grain grow
as high as my shoulder.

945
00:39:48,520 --> 00:39:49,655
Now, where is she?

946
00:39:49,688 --> 00:39:52,023
We want to take her back.

947
00:39:52,057 --> 00:39:54,193
I'll give you
your annikki.

948
00:39:54,227 --> 00:39:56,562
But it won't
do you much good.

949
00:39:56,595 --> 00:39:58,930
There isn't very much left
of your boat.

950
00:39:58,963 --> 00:40:00,767
D'oh--hey.
That's below the belt.

951
00:40:00,800 --> 00:40:02,535
Yeah, I don't really get
witches' humor.

952
00:40:02,568 --> 00:40:03,535
Mm-mm.

953
00:40:03,568 --> 00:40:06,672
Come along.
Let me show you.

954
00:40:06,705 --> 00:40:08,340
Brother.
She's got issues, huh?

955
00:40:08,373 --> 00:40:10,175
Mm.

956
00:40:12,177 --> 00:40:14,213
It's the swedish dells.

957
00:40:14,247 --> 00:40:17,650
The ducks. Ride the ducks.

958
00:40:17,683 --> 00:40:20,987
Hey. You wrecked our boat
you freaked-out maniac.

959
00:40:22,353 --> 00:40:25,323
A great fish
was swimming near the shore.

960
00:40:25,357 --> 00:40:26,492
Uh-huh.

961
00:40:26,525 --> 00:40:29,262
It flipped its tail once
and smashed your boat.

962
00:40:29,295 --> 00:40:31,297
Well I supposed those
kind of things ha--what?

963
00:40:31,330 --> 00:40:33,898
...i will make a new boat.
An iron one.

964
00:40:33,932 --> 00:40:36,168
And tell your fish
if he tries to smash this one

965
00:40:36,202 --> 00:40:37,503
it'll break his teeth off.

966
00:40:37,537 --> 00:40:39,772
Well,
you don't have to yell.

967
00:40:39,805 --> 00:40:42,273
Huh? What?

968
00:40:42,307 --> 00:40:43,975
They're roasting
bullwinkle.

969
00:40:44,008 --> 00:40:44,977
[Gasps]

970
00:40:45,010 --> 00:40:46,945
No.

971
00:40:50,048 --> 00:40:51,950
Save me, rocky.
Help me.

972
00:40:51,983 --> 00:40:53,885
Again?

973
00:40:53,918 --> 00:40:55,253
Oh, nobody ever helps
this guy.

974
00:40:55,287 --> 00:40:57,523
Look! A boat!

975
00:40:58,857 --> 00:41:02,495
Wuh-oh.
Outta control.

976
00:41:02,528 --> 00:41:04,263
[Gasps]

977
00:41:04,297 --> 00:41:05,932
What's going to become
of us now?

978
00:41:05,965 --> 00:41:07,867
Oh, everything's about you,
isn't it?

979
00:41:07,900 --> 00:41:10,335
When log flume rides
go horribly wrong.

980
00:41:10,368 --> 00:41:12,638
You may get burnt
on this ride.

981
00:41:13,938 --> 00:41:15,573
[Screams]

982
00:41:15,607 --> 00:41:17,877
Uh, there's a flaming moose
blocking traffic

983
00:41:17,910 --> 00:41:19,478
on i-35 w northbound.

984
00:41:19,512 --> 00:41:20,778
Would somebody
please put me out?

985
00:41:20,812 --> 00:41:22,047
I seem to be on fire.

986
00:41:23,748 --> 00:41:24,983
Protect us.

987
00:41:25,017 --> 00:41:26,752
Have mercy, dear mistress.
Chase it away.

988
00:41:26,785 --> 00:41:28,587
Do something.

989
00:41:28,620 --> 00:41:30,655
Now, there's something
you don't see everyday,
chauncey.

990
00:41:30,688 --> 00:41:31,690
Uh, what's that, edgar?

991
00:41:31,723 --> 00:41:33,225
Kiss goin' bass fishin'.

992
00:41:33,258 --> 00:41:34,293
Huh.

993
00:41:34,327 --> 00:41:35,693
Quite a boat,
wouldn't you say?

994
00:41:35,727 --> 00:41:36,695
Now that it's finished,

995
